  "b6_reason": "Carboxypeptidase is a zinc metalloenzyme, so its cofactor (prosthetic group) is zinc.",
  "b6_working": "Carboxypeptidase carries a tightly bound Zn2+ ion at its active site - the standard textbook example of a metal ion prosthetic group. Niacin is a precursor of NAD coenzymes, flavin of FAD/FMN, and haem is the prosthetic group of catalase/peroxidase and cytochromes, none of which belong to carboxypeptidase.",
